t": "a good night's sleep"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when you wake up in the morning feeling alert and refreshed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I just want a good night's sleep. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le08ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "therapeutic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "making you feel calm and relaxed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I find writing in a journal to be very therapeutic. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le08ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What haven't you done?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Talking about what you have not done"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Present Perfect in negative to express what experiences or things you haven't done."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject<br/>I/you/we/they <br/> He/she</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ auxiliary <br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">haven't</span> <br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">hasn't</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ <span class=\\\"underline\\\">past participle</span>*</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ complement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "*For irregular verbs you use the past participle.<br/>For regular verbs you add <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> at the end of the verb in the infinitive."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">haven't</span> <span class=\"underline\">drunk</span> any tea since I was in China."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">haven't</span> <span class=\"underline\">slept</span> for eight hours in ages!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She <span class=\"strong\">hasn't</span> <span class=\"underline\">cut</span> down her caffeine."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"strong\">haven't</span> <span class=\"underline\">started</span> a sleep diary."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Offering Advice and Solutions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can offer advice and solutions to people on how to improve their habits or well-being. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to offer advice politely and to use the modals <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to give a solution. <br/><br/>When offering advice and solutions, you can also use adverbs of manner to describe how something should be done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is a list of expressions you can use to offer advice and solutions:  <ul><li>You should ...</li> <li>You could ...</li> <li>You might ...</li> <li>You need to</li> <li>You ought to (strong request)</li> <li>You had better (strong request)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to cut down on the coffee slowly. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should drink more tea. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You need to think carefully. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'd better do this quickly."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le08ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find how a sleep diary looks like. How is the page organized?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a 5 day sleep diary for yourself using the example you f